SV CLI is an open-source, MIT-licensed command-line client for the SV API from SEO Vendor. Install it with pip install sv-cli (Python 3.9+) and the sv command gives you 16 SEO and GEO tools: SEO GPT and SEO GPT 2 content generation, content rewriting, SEO image generation, Better Keywords research, entity extraction, topical authority plans, competitor and page analysis, preliminary and GEO audits, SEO Strategist, SEO mapping, RankLens AI visibility, content quality scoring, top competitors and marketplace search. Output as pretty text, JSON, CSV, table or markdown. Async jobs support --wait and saved task IDs. Multi-agency profiles keep separate API keys per client. For AI coding agents, --strict --no-fuzzy --non-interactive --format json makes every call deterministic, and sv call sends raw API requests. Free API key.

SV MCP is a hosted Model Context Protocol server that gives AI agents direct access to the SV API from SEO Vendor. Point Claude, Cursor, Windsurf, Cline, Continue or any MCP 1.x host at https://mcp.seovendor.co and your assistant gains 15 SEO and GEO tools: SEO GPT content generation across 300+ content types, long-form articles with Prose, Better Keywords research with volume, CPC and intent, entity extraction, topical authority planning, competitor and page analysis, technical SEO and GEO audits, SEO mapping, RankLens AI brand visibility, E-E-A-T content scoring and marketplace search. Authentication runs on OAuth 2.1, so your API key never reaches the MCP host. Long-running jobs are polled for you, and wait mode returns finished results in the same conversation. It shares one core library with SV CLI and the REST API, so every interface behaves the same. Free API key.
